Predictive analytics, as part of the predictive maintenance process, identifies the increasing risk of equipment failure or failure of specific modules based on real-world data. Predictive analytics enables maintenance and preventative repairs based on predictions of the equipment's condition and remaining service life, rather than following a pre-planned schedule or after a failure.

Predictive analytics includes the following operations:

collecting data from sensors (temperature, vibration, pressure, voltage, current, etc.), collecting telemetry and operation logs, monitoring operating parameters (external factors and their time of action - external temperature, humidity, overload, etc.);

transmitting and storing data for subsequent analysis and statistics collection;

modeling and analytics using statistical methods, machine learning, time series analysis, anomaly detection, factor influence ranking, estimating mean time between failures, and predicting remaining service life;

solving an optimization problem for deciding whether to perform maintenance, taking into account the duration, scope, and cost of maintenance under various scenarios, service availability at specific locations and times, and other factors;

making management decisions about unscheduled maintenance and performing procedures for transferring equipment from operation to maintenance mode.
